    {
      "file": "Students suspicious behaviors detection dataset fo/Table_1.docx",
      "char_count": 2884,
      "preview": "Table 1 .   Dataset feature glossary Feature Name Data Type Description Example Values/Range Units (if applicable) face_present Integer (Binary) Indicator: 1 if a face is detected, 0 otherwise. 0, 1 N/A no_of_face Integer Number of faces detected in the frame. Typically 1 when  face_present  is 1. 0, 1 Count face_x ,  face_y Float X, Y coordinates of the top-left corner of the detected face bounding box. e.g., 260.7 - 318.1 Pixels face_w ,  face_h Float Width and Height of the detected face bounding box. e.g., 102.2 - 205.2 Pixels left_eye_x ,  left_eye_y Float X, Y coordinates of the left eye \u2019 s center. e.g., 281.2 - 370.5 Pixels right_eye_x ,  right_eye_y Float X, Y coordinates of the right eye \u2019 s center. e.g., 332.4 - 437.0 Pixels nose_tip_x ,  nose_tip_y Float X, Y coordinates of the nose tip. e.g., 272.6 - 415.9 Pixels mouth_x ,  mouth_y Float X, Y coordinates of the mouth center. e.g., 272.7 - 407.5 Pixels face_conf Float Confidence score (0-100) of the face detection. Higher is better. e.g., 50.2 - 97.8 Percentage hand_count Integer Number of hands detected in the frame. 0, 1, 2 Count left_hand_x ,  left_hand_y Float X, Y coordinates of the left hand. Zero if not detected."
    },
